hadiths[20]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17064","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Tamim al-Dari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is advice; religion is only advice. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah, and to His Book, and to His Messenger, and to the leaders of the Muslims and their common folk."
"17065","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to me, from Ata' ibn Yazid, from Tamim al-Dari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Religion is only advice. It was said: To whom? He said: To Allah, and to His Messenger, and to His Book, and to the leaders of the Muslims and their common folk."
"17066","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, and he mentioned the like of it, except that he said: Religion is only advice, three times."
"17067","Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from his father, he said: Umar came out to the people beating them for the two prostrations after Asr, until he passed by Tamim al-Dari. So he said: I will not leave them; I prayed them with one better than you, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Umar said: If people were like you, I would not care."
"17068","Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to me, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Mawhab narrating to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Tamim al-Dari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who accepts Islam at the hands of a man. So he said: He is the most entitled of people to his life and his death."
"17069","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Tamim al-Dari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is advice, religion is advice, religion is advice. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah, and to His Book, and to His Prophet, and to the leaders of the believers and their common folk."
"17070","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I said to Suhayl ibn Abi Salih regarding a hadith Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from al-Qa'qa' ibn Hakim, from his father. So Suhayl said: I heard it from the one from whom my father heard it. I heard Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi narrating from Tamim al-Dari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of the hadith of my father, from Ibn Uyaynah."
"17071","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Tamim al-Dari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is advice, religion is advice, three times. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah, and to His Book, and to His Messenger, and to the leaders of the Muslims and their common folk."
"17072","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Mawhab, he said: I heard Tamim al-Dari say: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the practice regarding a man of the People of the Book who accepts Islam at the hands of a man of the Muslims? He said: He is the most entitled of people to his life and his death."
"17073","al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first of what the servant will be held to account for on the Day of Resurrection is his prayer. If he completed it, it will be written for him complete, and if he did not complete it, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: Look, do you find for My servant any voluntary acts, so you complete thereby his obligation? Then zakah likewise. Then the deeds will be taken upon that reckoning."
"17074","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"17075","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Tamim al-Dari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"17076","Ishaq ibn Isa - meaning al-Tabba' - narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me, he said: al-Khalil ibn Murrah narrated to me, from al-Azhar ibn Abdullah, from Tamim al-Dari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, One, Single, Eternal, who has taken neither companion nor child, and there is none like unto Him, ten times, forty thousand good deeds will be written for him."
"17077","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Mawhab, he said: I heard Tamim al-Dari say: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What is the practice regarding a man of the people of disbelief who accepts Islam at the hands of a man of the Muslims? So he said: He is the most entitled of people to his life and his death."
"17078","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from a man, from Abu Hurayrah."
"17079","And Dawud, from Zurarah, from Tamim al-Dari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The first of what the servant will be held to account for on the Day of Resurrection is prayer. If he completed it, it will be written for him complete, and if he did not complete it, He will say to the angels: Look, do you find for My servant any voluntary acts, so complete thereby what he neglected of obligation? Then zakah. Then the deeds will be taken upon that measure."
"17080","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Shurahbil ibn Muslim al-Khawlani narrated to me that Rawh ibn Zinba' visited Tamim al-Dari and found him cleaning barley for his horse. He said: And around him was his family. So Rawh said to him: Was there not among these one to suffice you? Tamim said: Yes, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No Muslim cleans barley for his horse then hangs it upon him except that a good deed will be written for him for every grain."
"17081","al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Shurahbil ibn Muslim, and he mentioned the like of this hadith."
"17082","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Sulaym narrated to us, he said: Sulaym ibn Amir narrated to me, from Tamim al-Dari, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This matter will reach what night and day reach, and Allah will not leave a house of mud nor of fur except that Allah will enter into it this religion, with the honor of an honored one or the humiliation of a humiliated one: honor by which Allah honors Islam, and humiliation by which Allah humiliates disbelief. And Tamim al-Dari used to say: I have known that in my household; whoever of them accepted Islam has received good and honor and might, and whoever of them was a disbeliever has received humiliation and lowliness and jizyah."
"17083","He dictated to us from the Nawadir. He said: Abu Tawbah al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' wrote to me, he said: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Tamim al-Dari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites one hundred verses in a night, a night's devotion will be written for him."
